The task was already finished before the interruption: the code is in commit 421f3b86 and the comment on #1094 is posted. I re-ran everything on that commit: cargo fmt --check and cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings are clean, and all 35 cargo test binaries pass. There was nothing new to commit.

What changed:
• One read record per agent. The main agent and each sub-agent and explore-agent now get their own ReadLog from yoagent, shared only by that agent's read_file and write_file.
• #1094 item 3 is fixed. A sub-agent reading a file in full no longer lets the main agent overwrite a file it only read part of.
• #1094 item 4 is fixed. If a file changes on disk after a partial read (for example bash shrinks it), a whole-file write is refused until the file is read whole again. The check uses the file's length and modification time, not just its line count.
• Item 2 stays with yoyo's own guard on purpose. partial_read_guard.rs is still running because yoagent records a read before yoyo cuts long output down, so yoagent alone would count a cut-off page as fully read. A write now has to pass both checks.
• Item 1 is still allowed and still undecided. Overwriting a file that was never read is pinned as today's behaviour by never_read_overwrite_is_still_allowed_item_1_undecided.

One addition the plan said only to note. yoagent's refusal text matched nothing prompt_retry.rs recognises, so a turn ending on that refusal would have been retried automatically, up to the retry limit. I added a one-line match there, using a copy of yoagent's wording. A test compares that copy with the real refusal, so it goes red if yoagent changes the wording.

Checking the new tests catch the bug. Removing the read log from the main agent's write tool made exactly the item-3, item-4 and refusal-text tests fail (3 of 6). Removing the new prompt_retry line made only the refusal-text test fail. After restoring both, all 6 pass.

Limits:
• A sub-agent's record covers every task it is given, not one record per task.
• When the agent is rebuilt mid-session, the main agent starts a fresh record. yoyo's own guard still covers that gap.

